 "result": "{\"answer\": \"At perihelion \u2014 the closest point of Earth's orbit to the Sun, which occurs in early January each year \u2014 the Earth\u2013Sun distance is about 147.1 million kilometres (roughly 147,100,000 km, or 0.983 astronomical units; about 91.4 million miles). This compares with about 152.1 million km at aphelion in early July, and a mean distance of about 149.6 million km (1 AU). The exact value varies slightly from year to year, typically ranging between about 147.09 and 147.10 million km.\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"abstained\": false}",
